      "problem": "Factor the expression ${s}^{6}-4{s}^{5}+4{s}^{4}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, notice that all of the terms have a common factor of ${s}^{4}.$ To simplify the computation, we can factor out the ${s}^{4},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{6}-4{s}^{5}+4{s}^{4} & ={s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe expression ${s}^{2}-4s+4$ is a perfect square trinomial that can be factored as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+4) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}({s}^{2}-4s+{2}^{2}) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}({s}^{2}-2\\cdot 2\\cdot s+{2}^{2}) & = \\\\ {s}^{4}(s-2)^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
